    <%#
      讀法三's five spines and the twenty groups 康萬民 names along them.

      This figure needs its own group because it is not one reading among
      thirteen — it holds 3,518 of 起宗's 3,752 poems and 3,788 of Kang's 4,206.
      Nineteen poems in twenty are in here.

      Each spine is one walk along the lattice, read straight through in sevens.
      Each of the twenty 段 below is a window of four segments along a spine,
      which is one quatrain, and the label is the pair of characters Kang uses to
      name it: 智懷…湘津 is his own shorthand for "the reading that begins 智懷
      and ends 湘津". Picking one gives you exactly the poem he is pointing at.

      The line break is the thing to know about this figure. Its lines END on the
      lattice rather than starting there, so row 1 reads 智懷德聖虞唐眞 and not
      仁智懷德聖虞唐 — one cell of phase, and the difference between 讀法三之一's
      rhyme 真臣倫津 and 讀法一's 唐章皇湘. All twenty of Kang's start anchors
      sit at 2, 9, 16 or 23; not one sits on an intersection.
    %>
    <% third_spines = [
      [t("fun.xuanji.rules.kang_third_one",   default: "讀法三之一 首行轉右邊 — 七言七句"), "kang_third_one"],
      [t("fun.xuanji.rules.kang_third_two",   default: "讀法三之二 首列轉下邊 — 七言七句"), "kang_third_two"],
      [t("fun.xuanji.rules.kang_third_three", default: "讀法三之三 八行轉右邊 — 七言七句"), "kang_third_three"],
      [t("fun.xuanji.rules.kang_third_four",  default: "讀法三之四 中行轉右邊 — 七言七句"), "kang_third_four"],
      [t("fun.xuanji.rules.kang_third_five",  default: "讀法三之五 斜行轉下邊 — 七言七句"), "kang_third_five"]
    ] %>

    <%#
      讀法三's actual reading — 遞退 — and 附増第三圖's eight rays.

      遞退一句成章: a 段 is a sequence of seven-character lines and the poems are
      four-line windows sliding along it. 之一's 段 is thirty-two lines giving
      twenty-two poems, which is 88 原讀 ÷ 4 段. 之二's prints the same
      twenty-two entries with the same line counts over different characters, so
      the traversal is geometric and the two are transposes.

      All sixty-four lines of the two sequences end on a lattice crossing, and
      all twenty-two poems of each 段 rhyme on every line under 臻深通押 — which
      is 22 of 22 where 洪武正韻 gives 9. The selection of twenty-two windows out
      of twenty-nine available is NOT solved; see the controller's comment.

      附増第三圖 is eight rays from 心 at (15,15), and all 140 of its poems do
      resolve against the anchors Kang prints. The three readings below are his
